<title>UK: Glaxo in cooperation deal with Eukarion.</title>
<headline>Glaxo in cooperation deal with Eukarion.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glaxo Wellcome Plc said on Tuesday it had agreed a collaborative research and licence deal with U.S. company Eukarion Inc. to develop products to treat chronic diseases.</p>
<p>Glaxo, the world's largest drugs company, said Eukarion would receive funding, licence fees and milestone payments in additional to royalty payments for products arising from the cooperation.</p>
<p>Glaxo declined to put a specific figure on the cooperation but an official said it was on a small scale initially.</p>
<p>Glaxo said Eukarion was a small, privately-owned research company.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
